</gallery>

==Time Traveling==
The player can access events within two days beyond the current date. This can be acheived either by directly changing the device's current time, or manipulating its timezone, the latter of which allows you to move backwards in time freely. Certain conditions can result in an HGT error, including: setting your device's time to a point before your current time (e.g., going from 4:20PM to 2:30PM, applicable even in the event of "fixing" one's time, so long as the game detects the change in any way); switching timezones to one behind your current one (e.g., going from GMT+4 to GMT+3) before quickly closing the game; and moving beyond a specific threshold of time outside of the two day limit.

Do note that changing your device's timezone does not inherently cause an HGT error, but only triggers upon closing the game within around a minute of doing so. It is also important to note that timezones do not affect any cooldown and/or timer related events such as GAMATOTO expeditions, whereas changing your time directly does.

How to perform the glitch (by manipulating your timezone):
{{VideoGallery
|Rat3zeqSt14|<nowiki>The Battle Cats | Timezone Event Exploit</nowiki>
}}

==Mission Desync==
After changing a device's timezone, it is possible for timed [[Catnip Challenges]] to become desynchronized. This leads to some persisting well after they should have been cleared out and reset. The old missions will stay at 0:0 and can be finished normally. Any weekly missions completed in this state will still count towards the completion of the final weekly mission. The presence of the older missions may cause newer ones to not appear. For weekly missions however, the final reward can still be obtained if you manage to complete the requirements for the unseen mission(s). The problem can be resolved by transferring your save data to a fresh version of the app.
